<h1>{title}</h1>

<p class="lead">The word for <strong>water</strong> in Marathi is <strong>पाणी</strong> (pāṇī) — feminine, ends in ई, used constantly. This guide covers the word, drink phrases, polite requests, and the cultural habit of offering water first.</p>

<h2>Quick Answer</h2>
<table class="vocab-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Marathi</th><th>Transliteration</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>पाणी</td><td>pāṇī</td><td>Water (feminine)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>पाणी द्या करा</td><td>pāṇī dyā karā</td><td>Please give water</td></tr>
    <tr><td>पाणी मिळेल का?</td><td>pāṇī mīlēl kā?</td><td>Will I get water? / Is water available?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>थंड पाणी</td><td>ṭhaṇḍa pāṇī</td><td>Cold water</td></tr>
    <tr><td>गरम पाणी</td><td>garama pāṇī</td><td>Hot/warm water</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Grammar: पाणी is Feminine</h2>
<p>पाणी ends in ई → feminine. Adjectives and verbs agree:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>पाणी <em>थंड</em> आहे</strong> — The water is cold (neuter adj, but पानी feminine → थंडी in careful speech)</li>
  <li><strong>माझी पाणी</strong> — My water (माझी = feminine possessive)</li>
  <li><strong>पाणी द्या</strong> — Give water (द्या = feminine object imperative)</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip-box"><strong>Tip:</strong> In casual speech, adjectives often stay masculine (थंड पाणी), but possessives flip: <strong>माझी पाणी</strong>, <strong>तिची पाणी</strong>. Listen for the possessive — it's the reliable gender tell.</div>

<h2>Drink & Request Phrases</h2>
<table class="vocab-table">
  <thead><tr><th>English</th><th>Marathi</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Water, please</td><td>पाणी द्या करा</td><td>Polite imperative</td></tr>
    <tr><td>I want water</td><td>मला पाणी पाहिजे</td><td>मला + पाहिजे = need</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Is there water?</td><td>पाणी आहे का?</td><td>आहे का = is there?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cold water, please</td><td>थंड पाणी द्या करा</td><td>थंड = cold</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hot water for tea</td><td>चहासाठी गरम पाणी</td><td>साठी = for</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Drink water</td><td>पाणी प्या</td><td>प्या = drink (imperative)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Cultural Note: Water First</h2>
<p>In Maharashtra, guests are offered <strong>पाणी</strong> immediately — often before चहा (tea). Refusing is polite once, but accepting the second offer is expected. Say <em>हो, कृपया</em> (yes, please) or <em>पाणी द्या करा</em>.</p>

<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>❌ पाणि</strong> → <strong>✅ पाणी</strong> (long ई, not short इ)</li>
  <li><strong>❌ माझा पाणी</strong> → <strong>✅ माझी पाणी</strong> (feminine possessive)</li>
  <li><strong>❌ पाणी पीजिए</strong> → <strong>✅ पाणी प्या</strong> (Marathi verb, not Hindi)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Mini Practice</h2>
<ol>
  <li>"Cold water, please" → <em>थंड पाणी द्या करा</em></li>
  <li>"I need water" → <em>मला पाणी पाहिजे</em></li>
  <li>"My water" → <em>माझी पाणी</em></li>
</ol>

